<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">25 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 25 August, from 325 to 2012.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/first-council-of-nicaea" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-council-of-nicaea.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">325 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,701 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The First Council of Nicaea closes</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">By tradition the council summoned by Constantine ended on this date. It had condemned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arianism">Arianism</a>, adopted the Nicene Creed and set rules for dating Easter, shaping Christian doctrine for centuries.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1609">1609 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">417 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Galileo demonstrates his telescope to Venice's rulers</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galileo-galilei">Galileo</a> showed the Venetian authorities his improved telescope, which made distant ships visible hours before they could be seen by eye. The Republic rewarded him with a lifetime post at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/padua">Padua</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1825">1825 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">201 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Uruguay declares independence from Brazil</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A congress at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> declared the Banda Oriental independent of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Empire of Brazil</a> and united with the River Plate provinces. After a war, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruguay">Uruguay</a> became a sovereign state under the 1828 treaty.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruguay">Uruguay</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1919">1919 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">107 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">First daily international scheduled air service begins</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Aircraft Transport and Travel began daily flights between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>'s Hounslow Heath and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, carrying passengers, mail and goods. It was the start of scheduled international commercial aviation.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1944">1944 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">82 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Paris is liberated from German occupation</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">French and American troops entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> and the German commander, General von Choltitz, surrendered, having ignored Hitler's order to destroy the city. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-de-gaulle">De Gaulle</a> led a victory march the next day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2012">2012 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">14 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Neil Armstrong dies aged 82</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Neil Armstrong, the first person to walk on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhu">Moon</a>, died in Cincinnati after heart surgery. A modest engineer, he largely avoided the celebrity that followed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apollo">Apollo</a> 11.</p></div></li></ol>
